From: Stealth Build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 03/05] WebGL: never leak a software renderer

DESIGN (v146 CloakBrowser parity): the CyberPunch wrapper already spoofs
WebGL vendor/renderer PER PROFILE via JS injection (FingerprintDb). So this
native patch must NOT hard-pin one GPU for every profile -- that would
override the per-profile spoof and REDUCE realism. It is a guarded fallback:
return the REAL driver string unchanged (so the JS layer stays authoritative)
and ONLY substitute a common discrete GPU when the real renderer is a software
rasterizer (SwiftShader / llvmpipe / Mesa / Microsoft Basic Render), which is
the one thing that would betray a headless / GPU-less box.

VERIFIED against tag 151.0.7922.108: in v151 there is no GetUnmaskedString()
helper anymore; UNMASKED_VENDOR_WEBGL / UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL are served
inline inside WebGLRenderingContextBase::getParameter() via
WebGLAny(script_state, String(ContextGL()->GetString(GL_*))). We wrap those
two sites. String::LowerASCII()/Contains() and WebGLAny() are already in scope.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
@@ -4192,14 +4192,31 @@ ScriptValue WebGLRenderingContextBase::getParameter(ScriptState* script_state,
     case WebGLDebugRendererInfo::kUnmaskedRendererWebgl:
       if (ExtensionEnabled(kWebGLDebugRendererInfoName)) {
-        return WebGLAny(script_state,
-                        String(ContextGL()->GetString(GL_RENDERER)));
+        String real = String(ContextGL()->GetString(GL_RENDERER));
+        String lower = real.LowerASCII();
+        // Stealth: only rewrite when a software rasterizer would leak a
+        // headless / GPU-less box. Real GPUs pass through so the wrapper's
+        // per-profile spoof stays authoritative.
+        if (lower.Contains("swiftshader") || lower.Contains("llvmpipe") ||
+            lower.Contains("software") || lower.Contains("mesa") ||
+            lower.Contains("microsoft basic render")) {
+          real = String(
+              "ANGLE (NVIDIA, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Direct3D11 vs_5_0 "
+              "ps_5_0, D3D11)");
+        }
+        return WebGLAny(script_state, real);
       }
       SynthesizeGLError(
           GL_INVALID_ENUM, "getParameter",
           "invalid parameter name, WEBGL_debug_renderer_info not enabled");
       return ScriptValue::CreateNull(script_state->GetIsolate());
     case WebGLDebugRendererInfo::kUnmaskedVendorWebgl:
       if (ExtensionEnabled(kWebGLDebugRendererInfoName)) {
-        return WebGLAny(script_state,
-                        String(ContextGL()->GetString(GL_VENDOR)));
+        String real = String(ContextGL()->GetString(GL_VENDOR));
+        String lower = real.LowerASCII();
+        if (lower.Contains("swiftshader") || lower.Contains("llvmpipe") ||
+            lower.Contains("software") || lower.Contains("mesa") ||
+            lower.Contains("microsoft basic render")) {
+          real = String("Google Inc. (NVIDIA)");
+        }
+        return WebGLAny(script_state, real);
       }
